MoBetta: winemac.drv: Keep the hidden cursor inside the window during mouse-look.

WoW 3.3.5a turns the camera while a mouse button is held: it captures the
mouse, hides the cursor with SetCursor(NULL) and every frame warps the cursor
to (client origin + client size) / 2 instead of origin + size / 2. On Windows
the hidden cursor's position is never seen. On a Mac display left of the main
one that point lies ~1000 pixels outside the window, so the real, hidden Mac
cursor sits over other apps (their toolbars light up) and the frame rate drops
while dragging (MoBetta Session #20).

While the client hides the cursor and holds mouse capture, SetCursorPos now
moves only Wine's cursor position: the Mac cursor is detached from the mouse
(CGAssociateMouseAndMouseCursorPosition, as cursor clipping does), frozen
inside the capture window, and mouse movement reaches Wine as relative deltas.
GetCursorPos keeps the server's position, and button and wheel events carry
no position, while detached. Unhiding the cursor, releasing capture, cursor
clipping, a window drag or deactivating the app reattaches the cursor.

